ynasty. His rule coincided with a period of intense dynastic competition and the gradual Christianization of Ireland, during which Munster emerged as a significant political and cultural center. Cathal's reign laid foundational groundwork for the subsequent prominence of the Eóganachta in southern Ireland, influencing the political landscape for centuries.

